2013 ( [LINK: (MMXIII) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_numerals] ) was a  [LINK: (common year starting on Tuesday) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_year_starting_on_Tuesday]  of the  [LINK: (Gregorian calendar) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gregorian_calendar] , the 2013th year of the  [LINK: (Common Era) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_Era]  (CE) and  [LINK: (Anno Domini) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anno_Domini]  (AD) designations, the 13th  year of the  [LINK: (3rd millennium) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/3rd_millennium]  and the  [LINK: (21st century) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/21st_century] , and the  4th   year of the  [LINK: (2010s) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2010s]  decade.

2013 was the first year since 1987 (after 26 years) to contain four unique digits, or no repeating numbers. [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-theworld.org_unique_digits-1]

2013 was designated as:

International Year of Water Cooperation [LINK: ([2]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-United_Nations_Observances:_International_Years-2]

[LINK: (International Year of Quinoa) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Year_of_Quinoa]  [LINK: ([2]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-United_Nations_Observances:_International_Years-2]


# EVENTS #

[LINK: (January 5) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_5]  –  [LINK: (2013 Craig, Alaska earthquake) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013_Craig,_Alaska_earthquake] : A Mw 7.5 (Ms 7.7, 'Moderate') earthquake shakes  [LINK: (Prince of Wales Island) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prince_of_Wales_Island_(Alaska)] .

[LINK: (January 10) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_10]  – At least 130 people are killed and 270 are injured in  [LINK: (several bomb blasts in Pakistan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_2013_Pakistan_bombings] .

[LINK: (January 11) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_11]  – The  [LINK: (French military) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_Armed_Forces]  begins a 5-month intervention into the  [LINK: (Northern Mali conflict) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northern_Mali_conflict] , targeting the militant  [LINK: (Islamist) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Islamist]   [LINK: (Ansar Dine) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ansar_Dine]  group. [LINK: ([3]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-3]  [LINK: ([4]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-4]

[LINK: (January 16) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_16] – [LINK: (20) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_20]  – 39 international workers and 1 security guard die in a  [LINK: (hostage crisis) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_Amenas_hostage_crisis]  at a  [LINK: (natural gas) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_gas]  facility near  [LINK: (In Aménas) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_Am%C3%A9nas] , Algeria. [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-reuters1-5]  [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-6]  [LINK: ([7]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-7]  [LINK: ([8]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-8]

[LINK: (January 27) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_27]  – An estimated 245 people die in a  [LINK: (nightclub fire) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiss_nightclub_fire]  in  [LINK: (Santa Maria, Rio Grande do Sul) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santa_Maria,_Rio_Grande_do_Sul] , Brazil. [LINK: ([9]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-9]

[LINK: (February 10) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_10]  – Severe weather spawns eight tornadoes across southern  [LINK: (Mississippi) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mississippi]  and southwest  [LINK: (Alabama) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alabama] , including  [LINK: (an EF4 tornado which struck the city of Hattiesburg, Mississippi) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013_Hattiesburg_tornado] .

[LINK: (February 11) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_11]  – The  [LINK: (Emergency Alert Systems) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emergency_Alert_System]  of five different television stations across the U.S. states of  [LINK: (Montana) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montana] ,  [LINK: (Michigan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michigan] ,  [LINK: (Wisconsin) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wisconsin] , and  [LINK: (New Mexico) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Mexico]  are  [LINK: (hijacked, airing a false "Zombie apocalypse" hoax) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013_Emergency_Alert_System_hijackings] . It is amongst one of the largest cybersecurity breaches in EAS history. [LINK: ([10]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-10]  [LINK: ([11]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-11] [ [LINK: (importance?) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:What_Wikipedia_is_not#Encyclopedic_content] ]

[LINK: (February 12) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_12]  –  [LINK: (North Korea) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Korea]  conducts its  [LINK: (third underground nuclear test) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013_North_Korean_nuclear_test] , prompting widespread condemnation and tightened economic sanctions from the international community. [LINK: ([12]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-12]  [LINK: ([13]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-13]

[LINK: (February 15) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_15]  – A  [LINK: (meteor) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chelyabinsk_meteor]  explodes over the Russian city of  [LINK: (Chelyabinsk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chelyabinsk] , injuring 1,489–1,492 people and damaging over 4,300 buildings. It is the most powerful meteor to strike Earth's atmosphere  [LINK: (in over a century) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tunguska_event] . [LINK: ([14]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-14]  The incident, along with a coincidental  [LINK: (flyby of a larger asteroid) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2012_DA14] , prompts international concern regarding the  [LINK: (vulnerability of the planet to meteor strikes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Global_catastrophic_risk#Asteroid_impact] . [LINK: ([15]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-15]  [LINK: ([16]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-16]

[LINK: (February 21) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_21]  – American scientists use a  [LINK: (3D printer) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/3D_printer]  to create a living lab-grown  [LINK: (ear) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ear]  from  [LINK: (collagen) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Collagen]  and animal ear cell cultures. In the future, it is hoped that similar ears could be grown to order as  [LINK: (transplants) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Organ_transplant]  for human patients with ear trauma or amputation. [LINK: ([17]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-17]

[LINK: (February 25) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_25]  –  [LINK: (Park Geun-hye) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Park_Geun-hye]  becomes the first woman to become the president of  [LINK: (South Korea) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Korea] . [LINK: ([18]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-18]

[LINK: (February 28) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_28]  –  [LINK: (Benedict XVI) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pope_Benedict_XVI]   [LINK: (resigns) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Resignation_of_Pope_Benedict_XVI]  as  [LINK: (pope) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pope] , becoming the first to  [LINK: (do so) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Papal_resignation]  since  [LINK: (Gregory XII) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pope_Gregory_XII]  in  [LINK: (1415) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1415] , and the first to do so voluntarily since  [LINK: (Celestine V) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pope_Celestine_V]  in  [LINK: (1294) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1294] . [LINK: ([19]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-19]

[LINK: (March 13) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/March_13]  –  [LINK: (Cardinal) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cardinal_(Catholicism)]  Jorge Mario Bergoglio of  [LINK: (Argentina) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Argentina]  is  [LINK: (elected) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Papal_conclave,_2013]  the 266th pope, whereupon he takes the  [LINK: (name) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Papal_name]   [LINK: (Francis) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pope_Francis]  [LINK: ([20]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-20]  [LINK: ([21]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-21]  [LINK: ([22]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-22]  and becomes the first  [LINK: (Jesuit) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jesuit]  pope, the first pope from the Americas, and the first pope from the Southern Hemisphere. [LINK: ([23]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-23]

[LINK: (March 24) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/March_24]  –  [LINK: (Central African Republic) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Central_African_Republic]  President  [LINK: (François Bozizé) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fran%C3%A7ois_Boziz%C3%A9]  flees to the  [LINK: (Democratic Republic of the Congo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Republic_of_the_Congo] , after  [LINK: (rebel forces) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S%C3%A9l%C3%A9ka]   [LINK: (capture) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Central_African_Republic_Civil_War#Fall_of_Bangui]  the nation's capital,  [LINK: (Bangui) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bangui] . [LINK: ([24]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-BBC24march-24]  [LINK: ([25]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-AJE_CAR-25]

[LINK: (March 25) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/March_25]  – The European Union  [LINK: (agrees to a €10 billion economic bailout) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2012%E2%80%9313_Cypriot_financial_crisis]  for  [LINK: (Cyprus) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyprus] . The bailout loan will be equally split between the  [LINK: (European Financial Stabilisation Mechanism) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_Financial_Stabilisation_Mechanism] , the  [LINK: (European Financial Stability Facility) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_Financial_Stability_Facility] , and the  [LINK: (International Monetary Fund) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Monetary_Fund] . The deal precipitates a  [LINK: (banking crisis) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2012%E2%80%932013_Cypriot_financial_crisis]  in the island nation. [LINK: ([26]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-26]  [LINK: ([27]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-Eurogroup_bailout_package_agreement_on_25_March-27]

[LINK: (April 2) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/April_2]  – The  [LINK: (United Nations General Assembly) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations_General_Assembly]  adopts the  [LINK: (Arms Trade Treaty) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arms_Trade_Treaty]  to regulate the international trade of  [LINK: (conventional weapons) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conventional_weapon] . [LINK: ([28]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-28]

