[LINK: (Moldovan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moldova] - [LINK: (flagged) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ship_registration]   [LINK: (cargo ship) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cargo_ship]   [LINK: (MV Rhosus) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MV_Rhosus]  makes port in  [LINK: (Beirut, Lebanon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beirut,_Lebanon] , carrying 2,750 tonnes of  [LINK: (ammonium nitrate) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ammonium_nitrate] . After inspection by port state control, the Rhosus is deemed  [LINK: (unseaworthy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seakeeping] , and is forbidden to set sail. By order of an Urgent Matters judge in Beirut, the cargo is brought ashore in  [LINK: (2014) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2014]  and placed in Warehouse 12 at the port, where it will remain for six years. The ammonium nitrate will erupt in a  [LINK: (massive explosion) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_Beirut_explosion]  on  [LINK: (August 4) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/August_4] ,  [LINK: (2020) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020] . [LINK: ([77]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-rhosus.shiparrested-77]  [LINK: ([78]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-rhosus.bbc-78]

[LINK: (November 24) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/November_24]  –  [LINK: (Iran) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran]   [LINK: (agrees) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geneva_interim_agreement_on_the_Iranian_nuclear_program]  to limit their  [LINK: (nuclear development program) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuclear_program_of_Iran]  in exchange for sanctions relief. [LINK: ([79]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-79]  [LINK: ([80]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-80]

[LINK: (November 29) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/November_29]  – A police helicopter  [LINK: (crashes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013_Glasgow_helicopter_crash]  into The Clutha, a pub in  [LINK: (Glasgow) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glasgow] , Scotland, killing 10 people and injuring 31.

[LINK: (December 7) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/December_7]  –  [LINK: (Ninth Ministerial Conference) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Trade_Organization_Ministerial_Conference_of_2013]  of the  [LINK: (World Trade Organization) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Trade_Organization]  delegates sign the  [LINK: (Bali Package) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bali_Package]  agreement aimed at loosening global  [LINK: (trade barriers) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trade_barrier] . [LINK: ([81]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-bbc2-81]

[LINK: (December 14) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/December_14]  –  [LINK: (Chinese) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China_National_Space_Administration]  uncrewed spacecraft  [LINK: (Chang'e 3) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chang%27e_3] , carrying the  [LINK: (Yutu) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yutu_(rover)]   [LINK: (rover) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lunar_rover] , becomes the first spacecraft to "soft"- [LINK: (land) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moon_landing]  on the  [LINK: (Moon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moon]  since  [LINK: (1976) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luna_24]  and the third ever robotic rover to do so. [LINK: ([82]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-82]

[LINK: (December 15) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/December_15]  – Fighting between ethnic  [LINK: (Dinka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dinka_people]  and  [LINK: (Nuer) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuer_people]  members of the presidential guard break out in  [LINK: (Juba) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juba] , South Sudan, plunging the country into  [LINK: (civil war) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Sudanese_Civil_War] . [LINK: ([83]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013#cite_note-83]


